Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:10:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 286/289] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on keeping queued
 notes through a reload

Review fixes to the previous patch (2026-11-01).

Split view runs each pane as a same-origin frame in one tab, and those
frames share one sessionStorage, so every pane wrote the same queue
document and tab id: panes overwrote each other's notes, and a pane reload
found the lock held by a sibling and deleted every pane's notes with a
false "other tab" toast. A split pane now suffixes the storage key and the
tab-id key (and so the lock name) with its frame name, which the frame
keeps across a reload; the /split parent keeps the plain keys.

Ownership is now per note, not per document. Each stored note carries the
user it was queued under (null when identity was not known yet), and a
write never relabels it. At restore a note of the verified current user is
owned, a note of another user is dropped and counted, a note of a user the
page cannot verify is carried through every write untouched and never
restored, and a note queued before identity was known comes back only as a
Retry.

Attachment names kept in module memory by stable id are merged back into
every write, so a second reload still names the attachments. Only this
page's own lock wait running out counts as another tab; any other lock
error takes the no-Web-Locks path. A tab whose lock another tab holds no
longer deletes the notes: they come back waiting for Retry, with a toast
that is true either way. Removed notes drop their first-seen time, and the
toast no longer pluralises "had" with itself. New tests cover split panes,
the identity cases, two reloads with attachments and a lock error.
